WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:09.039
We have feedback from some six or seven committees
this morning, and I am going to invite the

00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:14.280
Chairs of the respective committees to speak
about the brief reports that we have in the

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.280
papers.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.330
Ed, may we turn to you in relation to the
Audit committee?

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:26.540
Audit committee
Ed Smith: In terms of progress, we have made

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:36.649
good progress in setting up a steering group
and a process to look at the information technology

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:41.460
governance to support Tim and the ISCG in
its work.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:48.129
I think that will be reported formally in
terms of its conclusions to a future Board.

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:52.800
In terms of the risks during the course of
the year and projecting to the year-end, we

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.030
are monitoring those.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:01:00.399
The one that I think we just need to raise
and monitor a bit more closely is the transfer

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:08.210
of balances from the old system to the new
system, and we are having fairly intense discussions

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:14.040
with the Department for Health about the obligations
they have to send us the information for the

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:20.540
legacy balances so that we can make sure that
we start our own system with the right and

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.000
accurate information.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.810
That is quite tricky, and we are probably
going to have to put some additional resource

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.270
into getting that sorted out.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.380
There is nothing else.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:38.360
We are up and running with full internal audit
and now a good reporting of financial information

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.820
through to the F&amp;I committee.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.290
I am happy to take any questions.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.540
Malcolm Grant: Any questions to Ed?

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.540
No?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:50.150
Thank you very much.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:58.060
Efficiency Controls committee
Paul Baumann: I have nothing to add to the

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:01.730
report as it is laid here, so I am happy to
take questions.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.500
Otherwise, it is all moving along.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.000
Malcolm Grant: Any questions for Paul?

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.000
No?

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Thank you.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.850
Finance and Investment committee
Ed Smith: There is nothing I would like to

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.150
add to Moira's report.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:26.390
This committee does now meet regularly and
has a pretty full agenda, but there is nothing

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:29.120
in addition to what has been reported in the
paper.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.120
Malcolm Grant: Thank you.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.300
Commissioning Support committee
Margaret Casely-Hayford: As has been said,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:45.319
the commissioning support committee has overseen
the performance of the commissioning support

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:48.270
units over the relevant period, and has seen
some good results.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:57.360
In fact, it is worth calling out that that
15 of the support units won new business to

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.910
the tune of 17 million over the period, which
I think is actually very heartening.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:08.099
And also that they are working together when
necessary to provide greater efficiencies,

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:13.050
which is also really worth noting.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:23.450
I think the one call out is that as the committees
looking to see the degree to which the support

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.670
units can gain independence.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:31.780
Autonomy throws forward some quite major issues,
and so the committee intends to get some more

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:37.599
work done, and will meet again before the
December board, and come back to the board

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:41.030
with further information about the options
regarding autonomy.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.530
New Congenital Heart Disease Review Board
Task and Finish Group

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:43.530
Overview
Malcolm Grant: Thank you.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.160
Any questions for Margaret?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.030
Well, thank you.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:53.950
In which case, may we then turn to the Congenital
Heart Disease Review Board Task and Finish

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.460
Group, which I will give a brief report on.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:00.381
The first thing to say is that we have had
two meetings of the Task and Finish Group

00:04:00.381 --> 00:04:05.739
since the last meeting of this board: one
was on 30th September, and the note of that

00:04:05.739 --> 00:04:11.520
meeting is in your papers; the second one
was more recently on 29th October, and we

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:16.160
have not yet got a formal note of that meeting,
but I will make one or two comments on it

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.550
as I report this morning.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:24.060
Just two or three things to which I would
wish to draw the attention of the board.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:30.010
The first is around the scope and the interdependencies
of the review that we are undertaking.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:37.270
You will see that our discussion in September
is outlined in paragraph five of the report

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:38.980
in front of you.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:47.449
But to update you at our meeting at the end
of October: we came to a view that the core

00:04:47.449 --> 00:04:52.530
of our review should be the whole lifetime
pathway of care for people with congenital

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:57.790
heart disease, and that provides us with a
clarity of approach for the review, which

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:02.760
we felt was not there previously.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:08.530
Interdependencies and the relationship between
child and adult were otherwise causing us,

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.660
I think, some problems of definition.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.770
I will ask in a moment whether Bruce wishes
to add anything to the discussion that we

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.770
had on that.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:20.310
Nature of working
Secondly, a discussion about the nature of

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.720
working of the Task and Finish Group.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:29.960
We were clear that we wanted to be open and
transparent in what we did, but that because

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:34.680
this was a small, informal Task and Finish
Group rather than a formal meeting of the

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:40.770
Board, we would continue to have our discussions
in a private and informal setting, but subject

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.540
always to a full report coming back to the
Board.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.419
I would have wished that the full report of
our second meeting were with us today, but

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:53.680
it just proved impossible to prepare that
in time to put out with the Board papers.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.460
Conflicts of interest
Thirdly, we have had a lengthy discussion

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.940
not only about the working of the Task and
Finish group itself, but of the reference

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:10.780
group and participation groups around it,
and, sensitive to the process on the previous

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:16.330
occasion of the Safe and Sustainable Review,
an absolute insistence upon proper handling

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:21.430
of conflicts of interest, of reporting conflicts
of interest, and of ensuring that the Chairs

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:25.419
of each of the different panels was alert
to potential conflicts of interest, that they

00:06:25.419 --> 00:06:31.080
were in the public domain, understanding that
this is an area of activity where conflict

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:37.250
of interest is almost inherent, because it
is a relatively small clinical community operating

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.350
here.

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:45.220
We just need to be absolutely clear that conflicts
are identified and that real conflicts of

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:51.600
interest are parked either by people not participating
in meetings or by being absolutely clear that

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:56.830
they representation in the meeting is not
of their particular provider, but of their

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:01.890
discipline and of the broader group that they
might represent.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:05.060
Timeline
The next issue that is worth touching upon

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.970
this morning is timeline.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:10.139
I am anxious that this should not drag on.

00:07:10.139 --> 00:07:17.699
I am absolutely committed to ensuring that
we make rapid progress and that we work across

00:07:17.699 --> 00:07:24.970
the whole provider sector in understanding
what is the national requirement for a service

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:31.509
for congenital heart disease, and that we
make progress with an ambition at the moment

00:07:31.509 --> 00:07:38.850
of coming back to this Board by the middle
of June next year with a firm and clear proposition.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:43.710
I think it will be a failure of justice to
all those who are affected by this review

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.340
if we fall short on that ambition.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:51.090
Whether that will be as crystalized and as
clear and as sharp as we would wish at this

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:58.310
stage, I really cannot promise, but we are
committed to doing this review at some pace.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:07.120
Finally, I just wanted to read out to the
full board the objectives that we have agreed

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:11.830
for the review, and just to ensure that you
have early notice of this and that they are

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:16.010
not going to await coming to the full board
in December.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:22.350
The first is to develop standards to give
improved outcomes, minimal variation and improved

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.290
patient experience.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:29.980
Secondly, that we should analyse the demand
for specialist inpatient congenital heart

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.770
disease care now and in the future.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:38.719
Thirdly, to make recommendations about the
function, the form and the capacity of services

00:08:38.719 --> 00:08:44.620
needed to meet that demand and to meet quality
standards, taking account of accessibility

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.140
and health impact.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:51.860
Fourthly, to make recommendations on the commissioning
and change management approach, including

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.770
an assessment of workforce and training needs.

00:08:54.770 --> 00:09:00.490
Fifthly, to establish a system for the provision
of information about the performance of congenital

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:06.890
heart disease services, to inform the commissioning
of these services, and patient choice.

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:11.339
And finally, to improve ante-natal and neo-natal
detection rates.

00:09:11.339 --> 00:09:18.270
So, these are high level objectives for the
review as a whole, and these are matters that

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:24.310
we will continue to carry through by use of
a programme board, by use of a clinical advisory

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:29.920
panel and by use of extensive stakeholder
participation and other engagement.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:35.330
So, let me pause at that point and invite
Bruce if there is anything he would wish to

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.330
add to that summary.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:40.430
Bruce Keogh: No thank you chairman, I think
that is very clear.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:43.680
Malcolm Grant: So, any questions on that?

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.340
Ciarán Devane: Can I make a small comment?

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:46.340
Malcolm Grant: Yes please.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:50.580
Ciarán Devane: There is an action in one
of the notes for yourself, chair, and exploring

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:56.510
the possibility of joint local government
engagement and working with the Overview and

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:57.510
Scrutiny committees.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:01.510
Where that works, it would be fantastic if
that could be achieved, because it can be

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:05.779
very helpful in the process as well, and particularly
if they can work together.

00:10:05.779 --> 00:10:07.850
Therefore, I would encourage that, if I could.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:08.850
Malcolm Grant: Thank you.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:09.850
We are fully committed to that.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:13.130
It is a shame Bill McCarthy is not with us
this morning, because he is taking the lead

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:17.810
on that and has initiated discussions with
the leadership of the LGA.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:24.269
We do accept that that is a fundamental basis
for future approach.

00:10:24.269 --> 00:10:31.660
We need to get as much convergence and consensus
of opinion across the provider sector and

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:37.160
across the Health and Wellbeing Boards as
we possibly can, to ensure that this is not

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:42.580
a tussle between providers, but this is moving
towards a nationally provided service of world-class

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:45.130
quality.

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:46.300
Thank you very much for that.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:51.180
May we then move to the Authorising and Assurance
committee report from Victor?

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:52.180
Authorisation and Assurance committee
Victor Adebowale: I do not have anything more

00:10:52.180 --> 00:11:02.420
to add to what is in the paper, other than
that we continue to move away from the authorisation

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:03.510
process into the assurance space with appropriate
speed.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:04.510
I do not know whether Barbara wants to add
anything.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.890
Barbara Hakin: It is in the paper.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:10.510
Malcolm Grant: Okay, it is in the paper.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:12.180
Any questions?

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:13.180
No?

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:16.360
Thank you very much.

